@* About.razor — public about / mission page *@
@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About — PwnLearn</PageTitle>

<div class="page-container">
    <header class="page-header">
        <h1>About PwnLearn</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="section section-alt about-hero">
        <p class="about-lead">
            PwnLearn is a free e-learning resource designed to enable students in non-computing fields
            at university to make their initial secure strides in the field of cybersecurity.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
            The platform closes the gap between curiosity and practical skill through structured modules,
            exposure to real-world tools and CTF-style challenges. With each lesson grounded in ethics,
            PwnLearn aims to develop a new generation of responsible, white-hat security practitioners.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Objectives</h2>
        <ul class="about-list">
            <li>Allow students to explore basic cybersecurity concepts and assess their interest before diving deeper.</li>
            <li>Provide guided exposure to an industry-standard toolchain — Kali Linux, Metasploit, and CTFtime — with structured hands-on exercises.</li>
            <li>Promote ethical security practices by framing all learning within a white-hat mindset.</li>
            <li>Emphasise responsible disclosure and legal boundaries throughout every course.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Platform Scope</h2>
        <div class="scope-grid">
            <div class="scope-col scope-col--in">
                <h3>✅ Included</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>User registration &amp; login</li>
                    <li>Course catalogue with modules &amp; progress tracking</li>
                    <li>Toolchain introduction pages (Kali, Metasploit, CTFtime)</li>
                    <li>Quiz and self-assessment for each module</li>
                    <li>Admin panel for content &amp; user management</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="scope-col scope-col--out">
                <h3>❌ Out of Scope</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Live VM / Sandbox environments</li>
                    <li>Real-time chat or peer-to-peer interaction</li>
                    <li>Payment system</li>
                    <li>Mobile or desktop app</li>
                    <li>Actual penetration testing infrastructure</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-alt">
        <h2>Toolchain Highlights</h2>
        <div class="tools-grid">
            <article class="tool-card">
                <div class="tool-card__icon">🐉</div>
                <h3>Kali Linux</h3>
                <p>The de-facto penetration testing distribution, pre-loaded with 600+ security tools and maintained by Offensive Security.</p>
                <a href="https://www.kali.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-external">kali.org ↗</a>
            </article>
            <article class="tool-card">
                <div class="tool-card__icon">⚡</div>
                <h3>Metasploit</h3>
                <p>The world's most widely used penetration testing framework — used by professionals for vulnerability assessment and exploit research.</p>
                <a href="https://www.metasploit.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-external">metasploit.com ↗</a>
            </article>
            <article class="tool-card">
                <div class="tool-card__icon">🚩</div>
                <h3>CTFtime</h3>
                <p>The central calendar and scoreboard for Capture-the-Flag competitions worldwide. Start competing and level up your practical skills.</p>
                <a href="https://ctftime.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-external">ctftime.org ↗</a>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
